#exile_letter.lua
He=
She=
Him=
Her=
him=
her=
His=
his=
Himself=
Herself=
himself=
herself=
May @1 name be forgotten.=
@1 is proscribed.=
Never suffer @1 to return.=
May the gods have mercy upon @1.=
Let none come to @1 aid.=
May @1 weeping never cease.=
@1 life is forfeit.=
It shall be as if @1 were never born.=
May @1 end be swift.=
May fortune forgive @1.=
@1 shall live so long as @2 deserves.=
Let the beasts do with @1 as they wish.=
This is justice.=
Let none dispute it.=
May @1 wander fruitlessly.=
May @1 bones bleach in the sun.=
May the worms feast on @1 flesh.=
May @1 suffering appease the gods.=
Let @1 struggling be without end.=
Let fate decide @1 destiny.=
May the land have pity and bury @1 disgraceful remains.=
Thus we declare.=
For we are merciful.=
Let this be our kindness to @1.=
Begone, evildoer.=
Thus do we cleanse ourselves.=
# Perhaps a reference to Pontius Pila
We wash our hands of @1.=
Fortune shall be @1 final judge.=
@1 is disowned.=
We never knew @1.=
@1 is cut off.=
Let @1 live with the beasts.=
Let the barbarians and wild folk have @1.=
@1 is not fit for civilised lands.=
# Perhaps a reference to Sheev Palpatine
Thus we ensure our security.=
Only the righteous belong among us.=
May @1 toil in vain.=
# Now a reference to Cecil B. DeMil
So it is written. So it is done.=
Even the dogs despise @1.=
We break no bread with traitors.=
Let this be @1 journey to cleanse @2.=
